Dear Samira,

Thank you for RFQ CVN-RFQ-26-1187 and CVN-SPC-3612 Rev X1. Our DFM review aga=
inst LPC-QM-021 Rev C (=C2=A74.6, =C2=A711.10) is complete; 11 items need you=
r decision (4 high risk: item 1: Polarity Method B with APC connectors; item =
3: LC/APC IL =E2=89=A4 0.15 dB, end to end =E2=89=A4 0.40 dB; item 7: OFNP pl=
enum rating; item 11: Samples in 3 weeks / 3,000 pcs by 2026-10-16):

 1. [R-03] Polarity Method B with APC connectors (risk: High)
    Your requirement: TIA-568 Method B, Type B cassettes
    LPC capability  : Method B mates key-up to key-up; with APC connectors th=
e 8=C2=B0 angles face the wrong way - Method B is only possible with UPC (LPC=
-QM-021 =C2=A74.6, =C2=A711.10).
    LPC proposal    : Method A (key-up / key-down, fibre n -> leg n) with Typ=
e A cassettes, or Method C. LPC proposes Method A.
    Impact          : Corvane to use Type A cassettes / adapters in the CX-HD=
 panel.

 2. [R-02] Elite-grade MPO-12 (risk: Medium)
    Your requirement: MPO-12 APC elite, IL =E2=89=A4 0.25 dB
    LPC capability  : MPO APC =E2=89=A4 0.35 dB Standard, =E2=89=A4 0.25 dB o=
nly with elite-grade ferrules (LPC-QM-021 =C2=A74.3). The approved MPO-12 kit=
 is standard grade; an elite MPO-12 kit needs a new supplier part incl. quali=
fication (8 weeks, =C2=A710).
    LPC proposal    : Standard-grade MPO-12 APC female, =E2=89=A4 0.35 dB ran=
dom mate.
    Impact          : Corvane link budget to use 0.35 dB per MPO.

 3. [R-04] LC/APC IL =E2=89=A4 0.15 dB, end to end =E2=89=A4 0.40 dB (risk: H=
igh)
    Your requirement: LC =E2=89=A4 0.15 dB; end to end =E2=89=A4 0.40 dB
    LPC capability  : LC/APC =E2=89=A4 0.25 dB Standard (grade B), =E2=89=A4 =
0.15 dB Best with grade A low-loss ferrules and 100 % end-face geometry (=C2=
=A74.6). The two connector losses add (=C2=A711.10).
    LPC proposal    : LC/APC grade B =E2=89=A4 0.25 dB; end to end =E2=89=A4 =
0.60 dB per fibre (MPO 0.35 + LC 0.25), typically =E2=89=A4 0.30 dB.
    Impact          : Grade A ferrules and 100 % geometry would add approx. U=
SD 35 per assembly.

 4. [R-05] RL =E2=89=A5 65 dB (risk: Low)
    Your requirement: =E2=89=A5 65 dB both ends
    LPC capability  : LC/APC and MPO APC =E2=89=A5 60 dB Standard, =E2=89=A5 =
65 dB Best (=C2=A74.3, =C2=A74.6).
    LPC proposal    : =E2=89=A5 60 dB both ends (typical > 65 dB).
    Impact          : None for DR4 / DR8 optics (=E2=89=A5 26 dB required).

 5. [R-06] 100 % LC end-face geometry (risk: Medium)
    Your requirement: 100 % geometry measurement, data per serial
    LPC capability  : End-face geometry IEC 61755-3-2: 1 per polishing fixtur=
e Standard; 100 % only as Best capability (=C2=A74.6).
    LPC proposal    : Geometry measured on 1 connector per 24-connector fixtu=
re; 100 % end-face inspection to IEC 61300-3-35; IL / RL per fibre in the ser=
ial-number data file.
    Impact          : 100 % geometry would add approx. 18 min per assembly.

 6. [R-07] Leg length =C2=B1 10 mm (risk: Low)
    Your requirement: Legs 500 =C2=B1 10 mm; trunk 3.0 m + 50 / 0 mm
    LPC capability  : Leg length =C2=B1 20 mm Standard, =C2=B1 10 mm Best wit=
h 100 % length measurement; trunk + 50 / 0 mm Standard (=C2=A74.6).
    LPC proposal    : Legs 500 =C2=B1 20 mm; trunk 3.0 m + 50 / 0 mm.
    Impact          : None - legs are dressed in the panel.

 7. [R-08] OFNP plenum rating (risk: High)
    Your requirement: Trunk OFNP (UL 1651)
    LPC capability  : In-house jacketing is LSZH (IEC 60332-1-2); OFNP only w=
ith UL-listed purchased plenum cable, 8 weeks, not stocked (=C2=A74.6, =C2=A7=
8.2, =C2=A79).
    LPC proposal    : LSZH trunk jacket (data hall without plenum air space).=
 OFNP possible as an option with UL-listed cable (8 weeks, approx. + USD 7 pe=
r pc).
    Impact          : Corvane to confirm the installation is non-plenum.

 8. [R-01] G.652.D ribbon (risk: Low)
    Your requirement: G.652.D, three 12-fibre ribbons
    LPC capability  : LPC stocks 12-fibre ribbon in G.657.A2 (bend-insensitiv=
e, fully compatible with G.652.D) (=C2=A78.1).
    LPC proposal    : 12-fibre ribbon G.657.A2 (RM-FB-RB12-657).
    Impact          : Better bend performance in the panel; no cost impact.

 9. [R-09] Trunk pull 100 N (risk: Medium)
    Your requirement: 100 N during installation
    LPC capability  : Trunk tensile load =E2=89=A4 50 N with the aramid jacke=
t; up to 300 N only with a pulling grip on the MPO end (=C2=A74.6).
    LPC proposal    : =E2=89=A4 50 N (installation by hand, MPOs protected); =
pulling grip as an option.
    Impact          : Installation instruction: no pulling on the MPO boots.

10. [R-10] Ink-jet printing on the legs (risk: Low)
    Your requirement: Port number printed on every leg
    LPC capability  : Leg identification by printed wrap labels; no ink-jet p=
rinting on 2.0 mm tubing (=C2=A75, =C2=A711.8).
    LPC proposal    : Wrap label on every leg 30 mm behind the LC (P01-P36); =
flag label on the trunk 150 mm from the fan-out box.
    Impact          : No cost impact.

11. [R-15] Samples in 3 weeks / 3,000 pcs by 2026-10-16 (risk: High)
    Your requirement: 50 samples in 3 weeks; 3,000 by 2026-10-16
    LPC capability  : New fan-out box mould 4 weeks; LC / MPO kits 2-3 weeks =
(=C2=A710).
    LPC proposal    : 50 samples at Corvane 2026-09-18; 950 pcs 2026-09-29; 1=
,000 pcs 2026-10-13; 1,000 pcs 2026-10-27.
    Impact          : Samples 3 weeks and the last 1,000 pcs 11 days later th=
an requested.

Delivery plan: Samples 50 pcs at Corvane 2026-09-18; Lot 1 950 pcs at Corvane=
 2026-09-29; Lot 2 1,000 pcs at Corvane 2026-10-13; Lot 3 1,000 pcs at Corvan=
e 2026-10-27.
Unit price expected above your target of USD 150.00; NRE quoted separately.
Please confirm by 2026-07-22.

Best regards,
